Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:17:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat(audio): MCLA_AUDIO_BUFFER, an output buffer of a
 chosen size

rodio's own stream asks ALSA for a 100 ms buffer. MCLA_AUDIO_BUFFER=<frames>
plays rodio's mixer through a cpal stream of the game's own with that
fixed buffer instead, for a shorter delay; a device without f32 samples
or one that refuses the size falls back to rodio's stream. Off by
default: on the Retroid Pocket 6 through PipeWire a 1024-frame stream
opened without error and played nothing.
